  "query_preview": "..\nTropical Storm Choi-wan continues to move away from Anatahan and is\ninching closer to Alamagan, pivoting slowly to the north-northeast \nthrough Saturday. During this time, the wind field will continue to \nexpand, exposing Tinian and Saipan in Tropical Storm conditions a\nlittle longer, now through Saturday. As such, a Tropical Storm\nWarning remains in effect for Tinian and Saipan. While showers have \ntapered a little due to a dry slot overhead, rainbands that pummeled\nGuam and Rota earlier this morning are now being pulled toward \nTinian and Saipan, with more intense showers and thunderstorms \nexpected tonight. After a lull in showers and thunderstorms expires \nsoon, periods of rain, widespread heavy showers and some \nthunderstorms are expected to return and continue to pummel Tinian \nand Saipan tonight, to then taper down thereafter as Choi-wan moves \naway. Similar at Guam and Rota, albeit only patchy showers and some \nthunderstorms expected overnight brought by very fresh to strong \nsouthwesterlies. A drier monsoon pattern will return early next week,\nwith low-end scattered showers and a thunderstorm or two expected to\ndevelop through next Friday. For more information, please refer to\nthe local statement issued by the National Weather Service under WMO\nheader WTPQ82 PGUM.",
